OBSERVATIONS (not grounds for FAIL)
 O1 /proc/self/mountinfo in the container shows the host SOURCE paths of every bind (the user
    name, the worktree path, the scratch path). This is metadata only, but it leaves the machine.
 O2 classify/tools read every string field of an error/turn.failed event, not only the message:
    {"type":"error","message":"boom","request_id":"req_4291"} -> quota. This only changes which
    skip reason is given.
 O3 exit 2 is also used when $SWARM_DIR/verdicts cannot be created, which is not a usage error.
 O4 codex.exclude lines are whitespace-stripped, and "  #x" counts as a comment. This mostly errs
    toward excluding more.
 O5 Plain-HTTP GETs to allowlisted hosts are forwarded (GET / Host: chatgpt.com -> 301). This is
    within the brief's CONNECT-only-443 wording.
 O6 A policy line without a trailing "/" does not exclude a directory's contents. CD4 docs should
    say "dir/".
 O7 Each oracle run leaves one dangling tinyproxy image (known). I removed mine by ID; container,
    network and volume counts are back to baseline (12/10/8).
